In this podcast interview, AI experts Aishwaria Raanti and Kiti Bottom discuss the fundamental shift required to build successful AI-driven products, contrasting them with traditional software through the lens of non-determinism and the agency-control trade-off. They argue that because large language models are probabilistic, developers must move away from rigid, one-click solutions and instead adopt a continuous calibration framework that prioritizes a problem-first approach over technical hype. To mitigate risks like unreliability and loss of user trust, they advocate for a step-by-step deployment strategy that begins with high human oversight and low autonomy, gradually increasing an agent's decision-making power as its behavior is proven. The conversation emphasizes that long-term success in the AI era depends less on being the first to market and more on cultivating technical flywheels, high-quality evaluative loops, and a leadership culture willing to rebuild its intuition through hands-on experimentation.